gtk-nocsd (4.8-1+unity5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * d/p/0001: a popped-out AdwDialog is closed when its parent window is
    destroyed, as an embedded dialog goes with its window ("closed" is
    emitted once). It used to stay a toplevel window and keep the parent
    window and the application alive; Epiphany, quit with SIGTERM while its
    "Set as Default Browser?" dialog was open, aborted on its check that
    the shell is gone.
  * Build-time test of the above under xvfb-run with the built library
    preloaded (debian/tests-src).

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:15:26 +0000

gtk-nocsd (4.8-1+unity4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Preload the library by path, /usr/$LIB/libgtk-nocsd.so.0, in
    environment.d and in /etc/X11/Xsession.d/51gtk-nocsd. The library no
    longer carries the setuid bit (mode 0644); the matching lintian
    overrides are removed.
  * debian/51gtk-nocsd: separate LD_PRELOAD entries with ':' only (spaces,
    tabs and newlines in an inherited value broke the session start), write
    the bare names of earlier releases as paths, read the systemd user
    manager's value in the form systemctl prints it, and add nothing when
    an environment.d/50-gtk-nocsd.conf of the administrator or the user
    turns gtk-nocsd off. Tested at build time under dash and bash.
  * Log out and back in after the upgrade.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:20:02 +0000

gtk-nocsd (4.8-1+unity3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * debian/51gtk-nocsd: start from the systemd user manager's LD_PRELOAD when
    the session has none. The session's value is exported to the user
    manager afterwards and replaced the one built from environment.d, so
    libunity-gtk4-menu.so.0 was dropped from Unity sessions and GTK4
    applications lost their global menu and HUD.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:37:09 +0000

gtk-nocsd (4.8-1+unity2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add /etc/X11/Xsession.d/51gtk-nocsd: environment.d only reaches the
    systemd user manager, so X sessions started from Xsession without it
    (Xfce, MATE, LXQt, window managers) did not load gtk-nocsd after 4.8-1
    removed the gtk3-nocsd Xsession scripts. It adds the library to
    LD_PRELOAD unless it is there already, and passes it past a setgid
    ssh-agent the way 70gtk3-nocsd-propagate-LD_PRELOAD did.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:19:37 +0000

gtk-nocsd (4.8-1+unity1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Rebase on Debian 4.8-1 (the version in 26.10). Fixes Chromium-based
    browsers losing their window buttons under Unity: gtk-nocsd emptied
    the decoration layout in the settings of the hidden window Chromium
    creates to read GTK settings (upstream ecd66fe, codeberg #67; LP: #2158965).
  * Drop our two crash handler backports (d851645, 664d8c6): part of 4.0.

